pan/bi: treat TLS stores as helper-generating in the helper analysis

The helper-invocation analysis tracks which SSA values need helper threads
alive. It does not follow values through memory, so a value that is stored
into a thread-local variable and loaded back later is treated as if it never
required helpers: the store is an ordinary message instruction, and the load
is a fresh definition. A shader that spills a derivative-derived value (or
keeps it in a TLS variable across the point where helpers would otherwise be
terminated) can therefore have helpers killed too early and read incorrect
values back.

Fix it the conservative way: any store into the thread-local segment counts
as requiring helpers, so its sources join the dependency set. This matches
the common nir_opt_load_skip_helpers behaviour that Kraid relies on.

DXVK hits this with the same class of spilling shaders as the forced-TLS
access hint: a value that should be helper-dependent survives in storage and
comes back wrong, which reads as NaN/Inf in the lighting/exposure path and
tonemaps to a white frame.

Ported from upstream Mesa 45ea3ed8 ("pan/bi: handle tls-stores in helper
analysis"), which is not in the pinned Mesa tree.

diff --git a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_helper_invocations.c b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_helper_invocations.c
--- a/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_helper_invocations.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/compiler/bifrost/bi_helper_invocations.c
@@ -1,5 +1,6 @@
